// example_attr_naked_method_non_asm_body.mir — confirms the sema-level "'@naked' function
// contains a non-'asm' statement" warning (see example_attr_naked_non_asm_body.mir) now
// fires for a method too, proving validate_common_attributes actually runs for methods. The
// overall build still fails, but for an unrelated, pre-existing reason (see
// example_attr_naked_method.mir): every method has a mandatory 'self' argument that LLVM's
// 'naked' attribute forbids referencing at all, so no '@naked' method can pass LLVM
// verification regardless of its body's contents.
//
// Expected: the sema warning is printed to stderr —
//   warning: '@naked' function contains a non-'asm' statement; naked functions should contain
//            only inline 'asm' blocks, since the compiler emits no prologue/epilogue for them
// — followed by a build failure from LLVM verification ('cannot use argument of naked function').

type Point = struct {
    x: i32
}

impl Point {
    @naked
    pub fn raw(self) {
        const x := 1
        asm {
            ret
        }
    }
}

pub fn main() {
}
